<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian import prices down 0.3 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian import prices down 0.3 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian import prices fell 0.3 percent in October to be 6.1 percent lower than a year before, The Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The rise in the value of the Australian dollar against a number of the major trading currencies led to a small decrease in the index in October,&quot; the bureau said.</p>
<p>Vehicles, fertilisers, minerals and inorganic chemicals were the biggest contributors to the fall.</p>
<p>The annual rate of import inflation bottomed at minus 9.7 percent in June and July.</p>
<p>It has been rising steadily since then.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
